  "description": "A parametric STOOL on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nONE OBJECT FOR THREE JOBS. A kitchen stool at 650 mm, a bar stool at 750 and a dressing stool at 450 are the same four legs and one seat at different heights — so this is one flow with a seat-height parameter, and the footrest simply goes to zero when it is not wanted.\n\nROUND OR SQUARE SEAT, two geometries. Square is a quad row; Round is a 24-point ring on the smaller of the two plan dimensions. Both sit on the same legs, which are placed by the leg size rather than the seat shape — so a round seat on square legs, which is what most stools are.\n\nTHE PUBLISHED COUNTER GAP is the 300 mm most people want between a seat and the underside of the counter above it. Subtract it from the counter height and you have the seat height to type in.",
